From 1b86f64a4a6a4d1a83eb5c22c02f0c45cf1b5566 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:46:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): Carvera names a smoothing ask instead of dropping
 it

The Carvera post never read the Smoothing / SmoothingMode PARAMs (#616),
so a document with per-operation smoothing on posted no word and no note.
The Carvera firmware's supported-codes tables list no blending or
smoothing word, so the post now writes the one-time
"SMOOTHING NOT WRITTEN - NO CARVERA FORM STATED" comment, placed like
the Mazak note (end of the section preamble), and nothing else changes.
Smoothing off stays byte-identical (the Carvera golden is unchanged).

Pinned by smoothing.rs carvera_names_the_ask_once_and_otherwise_posts_the_off_program.

Fixes #757

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
